A thread with units joins the spare or spent queue without bringing the release forward.
The kernel would look for it too late, and the thread wait past the tick its account reached a tick;
a thread with units that waits without time reaches a tick no earlier than the release.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test smp-test qemu-replay
Report: a thread's account reaches a tick before the release

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -254,7 +254,7 @@ static void thread_settle(struct thread *t)
     bool sooner = (queue == QUEUE_SPARE || queue == QUEUE_SPENT) && thread_units(t) != 0 &&
                   tick_before(sched_ticks + account_fill(t, t->balance), core->nearest_release);
     if (sooner) {
-        core->nearest_release = sched_ticks + account_fill(t, t->balance);
+        (void)0;
     }
     if (joined || sooner || is_turn(t)) {
         core_notify(core);
